{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":191,"output":1028,"cacheRead":24320,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":953,"totalTokens":25539,"cost":{"input":0.00002865,"output":0.000514,"cacheRead":0.0007296,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00127225}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I understand the real outputs. Design:\n\n`AixArtifacts::for_fixture(fixture_dir, tool_binaries)` — hmm, the brief: \"generates real contents by invoking the provisioned tools in the fixture (process-boundary: assert on exit codes + produced files, never internals).\"\n\nPlan:\n\n1. Add a `GeneratedAixArtifacts` or extend design. Brief: \"Static `&'static str` fields remain for hermetic tests; production entry returns owned contents. `run_ablation` gains a generation step for the full arm. Real-tool generation must be opt-in (env or parameter) so CI without tool binaries still runs hermetically — fallback to current behavior.\"\n\nSo:\n- Keep `AixArtifacts` with static fields + `fixture_files()`.\n- Add `AixArtifacts::for_fixture(fixture_dir, tool_binaries) -> Result<AixArtifactsOwned, String>` or a new struct `OwnedAixArtifacts { llms_txt: String, managed_agents_md: String, tools_toml: String }`.\n\nHmm — simpler: make a struct with owned strings and a `fixture_files()`; `AixArtifacts` static version can convert via `.to_owned()`. Or make `AixArtifacts` generic over content? Minimal churn: define\n\n```rust\npub struct OwnedAixArtifacts { pub llms_txt: String, pub managed_agents_md: String, pub tools_toml: String }\n```\n\nwith `fixture_files()` too, and change `run_ablation` to take something with `.fixture_files()`. But run_ablation signature is used in tests with `&test_artifacts()`. Keep run_ablation taking `&AixArtifacts` (static) and have generated contents converted into `AixArtifacts`? Static requires leaking... `&'static str` can come from `Box::leak`. That's pragmatic: `for_fixture` returns owned, then a helper `AixArtifacts::from_owned(owned) -> AixArtifacts` that leaks strings (one-shot generation; leaking fine and documented). Hmm, but tests calling run_ablation with static keep working unchanged.\n\nActually cleaner: run_ablation takes `artifacts: &AixArtifacts` today. I'll add a separate owned struct and a leak conversion so run_ablation signature stays. Alternatively, generate contents eagerly and leak — acceptable for a harness invoked once per process.\n\nDesign of generation:\n\n```rust\npub fn for_fixture(fixture_dir: &Path, tool_binaries: &ToolBinaries) -> Result<AixArtifacts, String>\n```\n\nWait brief names it `AixArtifacts::for_fixture(fixture_dir, tool_binaries)` returning owned contents. I'll define:\n\n```rust\npub struct ToolBinaries { pub wai: PathBuf, pub genesis: PathBuf }  // or just paths\n```\n\nHmm, what does genesis binary generate llms.txt? Check the genesis binary CLI: does it have a subcommand for llms.txt generation? The brief says \"genesis's generate_llms_txt (genesis-vibes crate) yields the real llms.txt for the fixture tool set\" — \"for the fixture tool set\" implies we build ProjectMeta/ModuleEntry describing the dulce tool family (wai, genesis, ddl...) and call the crate function in-process? But \"process-boundary: assert on exit codes + produced files, never internals\" refers to invoking provisioned tools in the fixture. Hmm.\n\nActually maybe simpler and consistent: llms.txt generation via genesis-vibes crate API in-process (`generate_llms_txt(&ProjectMeta{...}, &[ModuleEntry...])` describing the dulce tool family with the fixture's tool set). The managed AGENTS.md via invoking `wai init --json` in the fixture dir and reading the produced AGENTS.md. tools.toml content is scenario-owned? No — corrupt-config scenario owns .genesis/tools.toml (fault injection). The full arm writes `.genesis/tools.toml` too — collision test covers that. For real generation, tools.toml content can be generated... by what? Maybe written from the tool_binaries list — we can construct it deterministically from the tool set (that's harness-owned configuration, not \"placeholder\"). The anti-goal is about llms.txt and AGENTS.md being placeholder; tools.toml lists the provisioned binaries — generated from the tool_binaries parameter, that's \"real\" in the sense it reflects actual binaries provisioned.\n\nLet me check what genesis has for tools.toml — is there a genesis subcommand? Check genesis CLI."}}
