l(&dir).ok();\n}\n```\n\nNow the implementation of run_ablation changes touches all test call sites. To keep step 1 commit small but compiling, I must do the enum refactor in step 1 (otherwise run_ablation can't gain the generation step). Yes — step 1 includes the AixSource refactor + for_fixture (AGENTS.md + tools.toml real; llms.txt still the static placeholder? no — llms_txt field would be...). Hmm, in step 1 commit, for_fixture needs to return something for llms_txt. Options: for_fixture in step 1 returns llms_txt: String::new()? Then the integration test (full arm passes via llms.txt check) would fail — but I don't add that test until step 2. But \"no placeholder content in the real path\" is the anti-goal for the FINAL state; intermediate commit with empty llms.txt is a red-state artifact... but commit 1 is supposed to be GREEN. A green intermediate with empty llms.txt in real path is fine as a stepping stone; step 2 commit fixes it.\n\nAlternatively, generate llms.txt via genesis::aix::generate_llms_txt in step 1 too and only add the test in step 2 — no, that collapses steps. I'll keep llms_txt empty in commit 1 (documented \"llms.txt wired in step 2\"), then real in commit 2. Actually cleaner: in commit 1, llms_txt = the static placeholder AIX? No—worse. Empty with TODO comment.\n\nHmm, actually wait. Let me reconsider: does the fixture_files with empty llms.txt break run_ablation full arm in the step-1 integration test? I won't add a full-arm integration test in commit 1. Only the for_fixture unit test asserting AGENTS.md content. tools.toml comes free from wai init — assert in commit 1 too (it's produced by wai init, real). Fine.\n\nPlan for commit 1 diff in src/ablation.rs:\n\n- header update\n- `use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};`\n- `ToolBinaries` + `discover_wai`\n- `AixSource` enum\n- `GeneratedAixArtifacts` with fixture_files()\n- `AixArtifacts::for_fixture` (wai init, harvest AGENTS.md + tools.toml; llms_txt: String::new() with TODO for step 2)\n- `gen